# 📋 Functional Programming

| Function   | Use                                                       |
| ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |
| `lambda`   | Creates an anonymous function for short operations.       |
| `map()`    | Applies a function to every element of an iterable.       |
| `filter()` | Selects elements that satisfy a given condition.          |
| `reduce()` | Combines all elements of an iterable into a single value. |




# 📋 OS Module Functions

| Function             | Use                                                 |
| -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |
| `os.getcwd()`        | Returns the current working directory.              |
| `os.chdir()`         | Changes the current working directory.              |
| `os.listdir()`       | Returns a list of files and folders in a directory. |
| `os.mkdir()`         | Creates a new directory.                            |
| `os.makedirs()`      | Creates multiple nested directories.                |
| `os.rmdir()`         | Removes an empty directory.                         |
| `os.removedirs()`    | Removes nested empty directories.                   |
| `os.remove()`        | Deletes a file.                                     |
| `os.rename()`        | Renames a file or directory.                        |
| `os.path.exists()`   | Checks whether a file or directory exists.          |
| `os.path.isfile()`   | Checks whether the path points to a file.           |
| `os.path.isdir()`    | Checks whether the path points to a directory.      |
| `os.path.join()`     | Joins multiple path components into a single path.  |
| `os.path.basename()` | Returns the file name from a path.                  |
| `os.path.dirname()`  | Returns the directory portion of a path.            |
| `os.path.abspath()`  | Returns the absolute path of a file or directory.   |
| `os.system()`        | Executes an operating system command.               |

